
{"id":"dc124d4f-12bd-46a0-af3e-d54ef4877480","object":"chat.completion","created":1793331450,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"\n\n```python\nenv_r = read_file(\"deepinfer/environ.py\")\nlog_r = read_file(\"deepinfer/logger.py\")\nst_r = read_file(\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\")\nenv = env_r[\"content\"]\nlog = log_r[\"content\"]\nstats = st_r[\"content\"]\n\n# ---- environ.py: helper and cached configuration entry ----\nif \"def _max_message_chars\" not in env:\n    helper = '''def _max_message_chars(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"未设置表示不限长；设置时须为可解析为 >= 32 的整数。\"\"\"\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        value = int(v)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ValueError(f\"invalid int value {v!r}, must be an integer >= 32\") from None\n    if value < 32:\n        raise ValueError(f\"{value!r} must be >= 32\")\n    return value\n\n\n'''\n    env = env.replace(\"_descriptors: dict[str, EnvVar[Any]] = {}\", helper + \"_descriptors: dict[str, EnvVar[Any]] = {}\", 1)\n\nif \"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\" not in env:\n    needle = \"    # -- Logging --\\n\"\n    entry = (\n        \"    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(_max_message_chars)\\n\"\n        '    \"\"\"普通诊断日志消息正文的最大字符数；未设置表示不限长。\"\"\"\\n'\n    )\n    if needle not in env:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"logging configuration section not found\")\n    env = env.replace(needle, needle + entry, 1)\n\n# ---- logger.py: formatter budget and default initialization ----\nif \"import copy\\n\" not in log:\n    log = log.replace(\"import datetime\\n\", \"import copy\\nimport datetime\\n\", 1)\nif \"from deepinfer import envs\" not in log:\n    log = log.replace(\n        \"from types import TracebackType\\n\",\n        \"from types import TracebackType\\n\\nfrom deepinfer import envs\\n\",\n        1,\n    )\n\nstart = log.index(\"class NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\")\nend = log.index(\"\\n\\n_root_logger = logging.getLogger\", start)\nnew_class = '''class NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    \"\"\"Adds logging prefix to newlines to align multi-line messages, optionally with microsecond precision.\n\n    若 use_color=True 且输出为 TTY，会给日志级别染色（不影响写入文件的纯净度）。\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if (\n                isinstance(max_message_chars, bool)\n                or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int)\n                or max_message_chars < 32\n            ):\n                raise ValueError(\n                    f\"max_message_chars must be an integer >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\"\n                )\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n\n    def formatTime(self, record: logging.LogRecord, datefmt: str | None = None) -> str:\n        if not self.high_precision:\n            # 调用 logging.Formatter 默认实现，保持原来的格式\n            return super().formatTime(record, datefmt)\n        # ===== 高精度模式：在普通 datefmt 基础上附加微秒 =====\n        base = time.strftime(datefmt or _DATE_FORMAT, self.converter(record.created))\n        return f\"{base}.{record.msecs * 1000:06.0f}\"\n\n    def _truncate_message(self, message: str, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        if budget is None or len(message) <= budget:\n            return message\n        if getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return message\n        marker = \"...<omitted>...\"\n        remaining = budget - len(marker)\n        head_len = (remaining + 1) // 2\n        tail_len = remaining - head_len\n        tail = message[-tail_len:] if tail_len else \"\"\n        return f\"{message[:head_len]}{marker}{tail}\"\n\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        full_message = record.getMessage()\n        message = self._truncate_message(full_message, record)\n        if message is not full_message:\n            # 不修改共享 LogRecord；后续完整处理器仍能取得原始 msg/args。\n            record = copy.copy(record)\n            record.msg = message\n            record.args = None\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\\\n\" in msg and message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\\\n\", \"\\\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n'''\nlog = log[:start] + new_class + log[end:]\n\nold_fmt = '''    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )'''\nnew_fmt = '''    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )'''\nif old_fmt in log:\n    log = log.replace(old_fmt, new_fmt, 1)\nelif \"max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\" not in log:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"default logger initialization not found\")\n\n# ---- stats_logger.py: mark queue-consumed statistics as complete ----\nold_stats = '''            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n'''\nnew_stats = '''            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n'''\nif old_stats in stats:\n    stats = stats.replace(old_stats, new_stats, 1)\nelif \"keep_full_message\" not in stats:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"stats log queue consumer not found\")\n\nwrites = []\nif env != env_r[\"content\"]:\n    writes.append(write_file(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", env, env_r[\"file_hash\"]))\nif log != log_r[\"content\"]:\n    writes.append(write_file(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", log, log_r[\"file_hash\"]))\nif stats != st_r[\"content\"]:\n    writes.append(write_file(\"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\", stats, st_r[\"file_hash\"]))\nprint(\"writes:\", len(writes))\n\nres = run_command([\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"], \".\")\nprint(\"PYTEST_RC\", res[\"rc\"])\nprint(res[\"stdout\"][-4000:])\nprint(res[\"stderr\"][-1000:])\n\ndiff_res = run_command(\n    [\"git\", \"diff\", \"--no-color\", \"--\", \"deepinfer/environ.py\", \"deepinfer/logger.py\", \"deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py\"],\n    \".\",\n)\ndiff_text = diff_res[\"stdout\"]\nprint(\"DIFF_RC\", diff_res[\"rc\"], \"DIFF_LEN\", len(diff_text))\nif diff_text.strip():\n    try:\n        current_patch = read_file(\"patch.diff\")\n        patch_hash = current_patch[\"file_hash\"]\n    except Exception:\n        patch_hash = \"\"\n    try:\n        patch_write = write_file(\"patch.diff\", diff_text, patch_hash)\n        print(\"PATCH_WRITE\", patch_write)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(\"PATCH_WRITE_ERROR\", repr(exc))\n\ntry:\n    existing_run_log = read_file(\"run.log\")\n    print(\"run.log present\", len(existing_run_log[\"content\"]))\nexcept Exception:\n    summary = \"DeepInfer cross-module logging task\\npytest rc=%s\\n%s\\n\" % (res[\"rc\"], res[\"stdout\"][-4000:])\n    try:\n        print(\"RUN_LOG_WRITE\", write_file(\"run.log\", summary, \"\"))\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(\"RUN_LOG_ERROR\", repr(exc))\n\nif res[\"rc\"] == 0:\n    update_plan([\n        {\"title\": \"Read required source files fully\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n        {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n        {\"title\": \"Implement config, formatter, stats extra\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n        {\"title\": \"Verify with pytest and generate patch/run.log\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    ])\n    final_answer(\n        \"Implemented DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS in deepinfer/environ.py, added the keyword-only message budget and safe record-copy truncation in deepinfer/logger.py, and marked stats queue messages with keep_full_message=True in deepinfer/engine/stats_logger.py. Final python -m pytest -q passed, and patch.diff was generated with the three-file diff.\"\n    )\nelse:\n    print(\"Final pytest failed; inspect the output above.\")\n```","reasoning_content":"We need continue. We have 1 request left? \"requests_left\":1, request_number 19. Need implement logger.py and stats_logger.py, run pytest, generate run.log and patch.diff, final answer within single action. But first_write already done for environ.py. Need apply edits to logger and stats. Must be efficient: one action can contain multiple tool calls, but output one Python block and STOP after it. Tools calls persist. We can do several operations in one block.\n\nLet's inspect current logger lines 33-110 already known; environ modified already has _max_message_chars and likely config item? Evidence shows environ lines 150-234 listing config but shown chunk may be old? It includes -- Logging section without DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS maybe because the excerpt truncated? It ended at multi-modal line, then rearm. Hmm search_code found no \"DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\" in deepinfer. Wait search returned [] before edit? Actually current progress changed_files environ.py; evidence ev-d07bed shows _max_message_chars helper added at top, but config item maybe added? Let's read environ lines around Logging and end, plus logger current, stats _log_worker, and maybe run status. Need do this action since only 1 request left? We need complete all. We can read via read_range calls in same block; but then cannot edit based on result until next action—no requests left? Request limit 20, currently 19, so this response is request 20 likely final. We must perform edits, tests, patch in this single action without seeing results. That's tough. However tool results not visible but can execute conditionally with Python using read_file results and string manipulation. We can programmatically patch files using read_file content and write_file with expected hashes, checking. We know files content hashes from full reads: logger 5b8f..., stats 9ef9..., environ 73cda... but environ changed after? Progress changed_files environ, yet file_hash in evidence equals original 73cda... maybe that's current? Hmm evidence hash same as registered full read 73cda... but changed_files says environ changed. Maybe they recorded exact hash? Actually if changed, hash should differ. The evidence ev-d07bed shows helper _max_message_chars added, so current hash likely different from registered? Wait registered full read environ hash 73cda7..., and evidence shows same hash with _max_message_chars helper. Maybe original environ already had helper? No original probably not; but maybe prior change replaced content resulting same? impossible. Maybe registered full read happened after change? Progress says full reads registered hash 73cda... and changed environ. Could be that first write changed to content with same hash? impossible. Perhaps initial read was after e.g. it already included helper? Not worry: can use read_file inside code to get actual current content and hash, then construct edits and write. Allowed in action code.\n\nNeed know logger full current text and stats. We have necessary snippets. Build patches programmatically robustly:\n\nLogger:\n- import environ envs? Check logger imports: logger.py lines 1-32 no `from deepinfer import envs`. We can add `from deepinfer import envs`. Potential circular? environ imports only os/threading/etc. Fine.\n- NewLineFormatter __init__ add `*, max_message_chars: int | None = None`; validate bool not accepted, int >=32. Need \"other values must be int >=32, bool not\". Use `if max_message_chars is not None: if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32: raise ValueError(...)`. Note int subclasses? bool only excluded.\n- format: need calculate message after `%s` substitution. `super().format(record)` sets record.message = record.getMessage() and formats. We must truncate only message with marker. Need preserve exception and stack info and prefix. Requirements:\n  - truncate after args substitution but not in shared record; use formatter internals. Best construct message ourselves: `record.getMessage()` (doesn't mutate msg/args, just reads). Then apply truncation to message. Then need render format with prefix using a copy? Logging.Formatter.format does `record.message = record.getMessage()` mutating record (allowed? requirement says cannot rewrite shared record's msg,args,exc_info,stack_info; setting record.message is arguably okay but could alter for later handlers? record.message normally set anyway by standard formatter. But if we copy record to avoid effect, safer). To keep exception traceback and stack_info but message truncated, we can temporarily set record.message then call super().format(record)? But super().format will recompute record.message = record.getMessage(), overwriting. Could use a shallow copy (`copy.copy(record)`) and set `msg`/`args` to truncated message? Standard Formatter.format does:\n```\nrecord.message = record.getMessage()\nif self.usesTime(): record.asctime = ...\ns = self.formatMessage(record)\nif record.exc_info:\n   if not record.exc_text: record.exc_text = self.formatException(record.exc_info)\nif record.exc_text: s = s + ...\nif record.stack_info: s = s + self.formatStack(...)\n```\nIf copy record with `msg=truncated`, `args=()` then getMessage returns truncated. `exc_info` preserved (we don't mutate). `stack_info` preserved. `record.message` original might not exist, later full handler fine. But copy.copy needs import copy (standard library). Alternatively use `record.getMessage()` to get full message, compute truncated, then temporarily set `record.msg = truncated; record.args = None` around super().format and restore in finally. Requirement \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\" could mean not permanently rewrite; temporary is risky. Use copy. But copy's exc_info etc same references not modified by formatting except exc_text maybe. `super().format(copy)` sets `exc_text` on copy only. Fine. However formatTime uses record converter; copy works.\n\nBut `NewLineFormatter.format` currently calls `super().format(record)` then uses `record.message` for newline alignment. We'll refactor:\n```\nfull_message = record.getMessage()\nmessage = self._truncate_message(full_message)\nif message != full_message:\n    record = copy.copy(record)\n    record.msg = message\n    record.args = None\nmsg = super().format(record)\nif \"\\n\" in msg and message:\n    prefix = msg[:msg.find(message)]\n...\n```\nIf message empty, existing behavior. For original no truncation, can still copy? We may avoid copy if no truncation to preserve exact behavior. But if truncation, copy and `message` matches. Note `getMessage()` handles args. If message includes `%`? okay.\n- Budget only message body, not prefix/exception/stack_info. Our approach does that.\n- marker length 15? `...<omitted>...` count: 3 + 9? Let's count: \"...<omitted>...\" = 3 dots + \"<omitted>\" 9 + 3 dots = 15. Budget min32, remaining >=17.\n- keep prefix ceil half of remaining: `head = (remaining + 1)//2`, tail = remaining //2. Example 32 remaining17 -> head9 tail8 correct.\n- if full contains newline, truncation after args substitution counts newline as char. fine.\n- keep_full_message exactly True: `if getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True: return full_message` no truncation. In format, determine message full; if keep true use full.\n- preserve high precision/color.\n- default setup: `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`; config item may not exist yet; ensure add to environ.\n- repeated initialization doesn't add handlers